description:
## Scope

This PR adds an exploratory design spike for `.mcp-console/config.yaml`. It is not a normative schema freeze or a complete pre-implementation security specification.

The design document is intentionally self-standing: it contains the review standard, the durable product and safety invariants, and the boundaries between what this spike settles and what later implementation PRs must define and test. Pull-request comments are not part of the configuration contract.

Review should focus on the simple user journey, progressive disclosure, terminology, major trust boundaries, and whether unsupported advanced combinations fail closed. Exact parser algorithms, provider protocols, platform enforcement, option allowlists, proxy canonicalization, cache locking, and similar mechanics are deliberately finalized alongside the implementation and tests for each feature.

## What this PR establishes

- compact built-in profiles with local scalar → sequence → mapping expansion;
- descriptor-style filesystem fields: `readable_roots`, `writable_roots`, `unreadable`, and `unwritable`;
- one profile as the complete user-facing description of a session;
- local, SSH, container, Docker Sandbox, and advanced runner directions without exposing a transport/compute graph to ordinary users;
- progressive R, Python, SQL, package-source, log, cache, resource, and environment configuration;
- trust-layer attribution, non-widenable higher-trust boundaries, and fail-closed handling for unimplemented security-sensitive combinations;
- a path from simple project files to reusable definitions only after repetition appears.

## Status

Advanced examples remain aspirational and may be revised, deferred, or removed as implementation work exposes better designs. The first implementation slices are expected to support a deliberately smaller subset of this format.

## Validation

- all 113 fenced YAML examples remain unchanged and retain the prior successful parsing validation;
- committed configuration document blob: `0e391274e4dd7bf9852ad8540a293befe98765af`;
- documentation-only changes across `design-sketches/CONFIGURATION.md` and `design-sketches/AGENTS.md`;
- all current review threads have specific replies and are resolved.
